+# Veterinarian Search Stays Out of Scope, but Filtering the Directory Is In
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined searching for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian, leaving owners as the only searchable records. The row was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey. Its provenance stayed part of the open Non-Goals consultation.
+
+A request to filter the veterinarian directory by specialty reached that row (2026-09-18). Read broadly, NG-9 declines any narrowing of the directory. Read narrowly, it declines only free-text search. The owner decided between the readings at intake.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-9 whole.** Decline the specialty filter as veterinarian search. Rejected by the owner.
+2. **Drop the veterinarian clause entirely.** This would open free-text veterinarian search as well. Rejected by the owner: free-text search stays out.
+3. **Narrow the veterinarian clause** (chosen). Free-text veterinarian search stays declined. Filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in scope.
+
+## Decision
+
+The owner decided (2026-09-18): "Non-goal NG-9 is narrowed: free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope, but filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in."
+
+NG-9 now declines free-text search for a veterinarian, and search of any kind for a pet or a visit. Filtering the veterinarian directory by an attribute it shows is not a non-goal. The specialty filter is the first such capability.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The specialty filter enters the PRD as a requirement of the veterinarian directory.
+- A request for typed-text veterinarian search still meets NG-9 and proceeds only on a fresh owner decision.
+- The pet and visit clauses of NG-9 are unchanged and stay part of the open provenance consultation.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed NG-9 row.
+- [PRD Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the specialty filter the narrowing admits.
